  "description": "Canonical corpus for the message-suppression predicate (is_suppressed / is_spam_by_classifier / is_text_blocked). This mirrors the webapp's isSpamByClassifier (src/stores/messages/predicates.ts, decision order: disabled -> promoted hash -> demoted hash -> hidden category -> hide_auto_beacons -> min_info_score) combined with the unconditional isTextBlocked half of passesBaseGuards. It exists because the server's unread-badge count used to count every stored message, including ones the client's own spam filter or blocklist would never render, which left a badge unclearable whenever the newest message in a conversation was hidden (doc/2026-09-19_2140-unread-suppression-plan.md). Field names in `policies` and `message` are the webapp's wire names (camelCase) so this file can be hand-copied there unchanged; MCProxy's own predicate uses snake_case internally and translates via policy_from_parts/view_from_row.",
